1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,120
ALL DEPICTED EVENTS ARE FICTIONAL

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,800
AND FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY.
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

3
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,960
Do you believe in multiple lifetimes?

4
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:25,520
Master Klao!

5
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,640
-What?
-Master!

6
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:28,000
Where am I?

7
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,480
<i>I too have been pondering</i>

8
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:31,680
<i>the circumstances that brought you here.</i>

9
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:33,600
<i>How the hell did I end up here?</i>

10
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,360
<i>What happened to me?</i>

11
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,680
<i>Look at the student sleeping there.</i>

12
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,840
Maybe he's already traveled back in time

13
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,040
to either the Sukhothai
or Ayutthaya period.

14
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,560
Students, what are common methods
for main characters

15
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,440
to travel back in time

16
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,080
and then return to the present?

17
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,960
Through a mirror.

18
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:26,600
Drowning and being transported
into a body in a another era.

19
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:29,440
Seeing one's past life
after donning traditional attire.

20
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,920
Those are interesting answers.

21
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
But sometimes, drifting off to sleep,

22
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,080
passing out,

23
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:41,920
or being knocked out by an accident

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,040
can make someone travel back in time.

25
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,240
When it comes to traveling back in time,

26
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:51,040
death is considered the starting point.

27
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:55,560
It's about dying
and traveling to a different realm,

28
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,080
then being reincarnated as someone else.

29
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:23,080
<i>Hey, go away.</i>

30
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,120
<i>I want to return to the present.</i>

31
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,080
<i>I'm telling you to go away!</i>

32
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,080
<i>This guy again.</i>

33
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,000
<i>Why am I still here?</i>

34
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:28,040
<i>I'm stuck in a loop.</i>

35
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:31,280
<i>Why didn't I die and return to the present</i>
<i>like the professor said?</i>

36
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:35,040
-Sterilized cloth, posthaste!
-Yes, my Lord.

37
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,880
<i>Gosh, you.</i>

38
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:40,200
<i>It's just a guy who got soaked.</i>
<i>No need to yell.</i>

39
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,600
As you requested, my Lord.

40
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,240
<i>Really?</i>

41
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:13,960
<i>Why is he patting me dry?</i>

42
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,640
<i>That tickles.</i>

43
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,800
<i>But if I open my eyes now,</i>
<i>I'll be screwed.</i>

44
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,560
Fetch your master fresh attire,

45
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:40,080
and summon all servants to the hall.

46
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:46,280
Tarry no longer,
for my indulgence has its limits.

47
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,120
Yes, my Lord.

48
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,600
<i>Wait.</i>

49
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:55,120
<i>"Fetch me fresh attire"?</i>
<i>I'm going to be naked?</i>

50
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,320
<i>Hey, don't you dare.</i>
<i>Don't do it.</i>

51
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,400
Don't!

52
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,240
Hey.

53
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,000
<i>You son of a rogue!</i>

54
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,600
<i>Father and son alike!</i>

55
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:24,240
<i>-Bastard.</i>
<i>-You son of a rogue!</i>

56
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,040
<i>You shall never prosper, Klao!</i>

57
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,720
<i>Father and son alike, wretched both!</i>

58
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,680
<i>Vile thing!</i>

59
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,880
<i>Scum!</i>

60
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,160
<i>You shall never prosper.</i>

61
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,880
<i>Whither do you think to escape me!</i>

62
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,400
A dream within a dream.

63
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:46,000
Am I dreaming, or is this real?

64
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,080
What is the matter, Master Klao?

65
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,840
<i>Okay, that hurts.</i>

66
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,160
<i>I'm not dreaming.</i>

67
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:16,680
<i>So I've traveled back in time.</i>

68
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:20,240
<i>The costumes… the manor…</i>
<i>I'm in the Ayutthaya period, right?</i>

69
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,880
<i>I drowned and passed out,</i>

70
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,320
<i>but I didn't return to the present.</i>

71
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,920
<i>So that's not my way out.</i>

72
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,720
<i>I want my iPad.</i>

73
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,400
<i>I need Wi-Fi.</i>

74
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,120
<i>I want to ask ChatGPT,</i>

75
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,960
<i>"How do I go back to the present?"</i>

76
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:44,320
<i>Who the hell dressed me up?</i>

77
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,040
Dear Klao's arrival
heralds not the conclusion.

78
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,880
You suffered him to slip away,

79
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,920
unbeknownst to any soul.

80
00:07:56,280 --> 00:08:00,000
Upon his return, you offered no comfort
as he sank into despair.

81
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,040
Chuay.

82
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:06,240
Have you discerned where he has gone?

83
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,840
Before he vanished,

84
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:10,920
he was last seen at the riverside market.

85
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,120
And he has been absent ever since.

86
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,640
Henceforth, provide him
with your utmost devotion

87
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,640
and maintain a vigilant watch over him,

88
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,240
especially you, Chuay.

89
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,560
Should any further misfortune befall him,

90
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,760
the caning shall be yours.

91
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,960
I fear a bitter cold has
taken hold of him.

92
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,240
Summon the physician at once.

93
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,360
Yes, my Lord.

94
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,440
Yes, my Lord.

95
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,960
I am aware of your wakefulness,

96
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:06,360
having heard every word
I spoke behind closed doors.

97
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,360
You yelled
as if the house were on fire.

98
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,680
Forgive me.

99
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,600
Do you wish to return to slumber?

100
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,840
I'm good.

101
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:23,840
Hey,

102
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,280
by the way,

103
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:28,000
did you put on new clothes for me?

104
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:29,760
Indeed.

105
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,520
What stirs your concern?

106
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,280
No, you can't just change
someone's clothes.

107
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,800
I didn't give my consent either.

108
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,520
What has caused this discord?

109
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,880
It was ever my hands
that clothed you in your youth.

110
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,480
Am I now a stranger in your eyes?

111
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,920
Well, you are a stranger to me…

112
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,320
Whether this be a lapse of memory
or the harboring of some silent grievance,

113
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:03,720
never repeat such displays of conduct.

114
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:06,440
Voice your concerns, should any arise.

115
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,800
Forsake not your life.

116
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:31,840
This way, Physician.
Waste no moment, for time is fleeting.

117
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,800
There's no need to hurry.

118
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:37,680
I believe he's hale and hearty.

119
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,880
Merely adrift in a sea of delusions.

120
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:57,440
Thee?!

121
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,480
Thee!

122
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,760
Hey, Thee!

123
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,080
-Seize Klao at once!
-Thee!

124
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,080
He has gone mad!

125
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:11,640
Master Klao.

126
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,360
You traveled through time to save me,

127
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,880
or are you pulling my leg?

128
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,080
Thee.

129
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,120
You've got the guts.

130
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,720
You always have what it takes.

131
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:45,640
I know your family's rich,

132
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,760
but I didn't expect you to go overboard.

133
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:51,600
At first,
I thought they were filming a series.

134
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,680
But when I looked around,
there were no cameras.

135
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,400
I've figured it out.

136
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:59,760
You're providing me
with an immersive experience, right?

137
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,040
Sheesh.

138
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,960
I knew it.

139
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:11,360
I saw you signaling.

140
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,280
I saw it.

141
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,480
You guys are busted.

142
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:19,440
Well played, guys.

143
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,320
He suffers not from the wild, Phop,

144
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,520
but from the spirits he has consumed.

145
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,000
I shall provide the remedy.

146
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,720
The remedy?

147
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,240
Hey.

148
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:39,000
What are you doing?

149
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,080
Expect a severe purging,

150
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,880
yet the remedy shall bring relief.

151
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,600
It shall restore his clarity and dignity.

152
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,800
What are you doing?

153
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:51,520
What the hell are you doing to me?

154
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,920
Spirits transmute a gentleman
into a vessel of madness.

155
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,640
Take this remedy at once, Klao.

156
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,480
Your condition will improve.

157
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:01,200
Look at you.
I'm gonna tell Pun about this.

158
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,080
And stop calling me Klao already.

159
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,240
It tastes like shit.

160
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:16,760
What did you just feed me?

161
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,280
Worry not,

162
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,560
for his recovery is assured.

163
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,280
Are you quite certain, Jom?

164
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,680
It appears his condition
is in further decline.

165
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,920
The remedy takes hold.

166
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:45,320
The expulsion is but the first step.

167
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:58,840
Does your skepticism remain, Phop?

168
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,880
Does it not strike you as strange

169
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:06,240
that he so adamantly denies
his own identity,

170
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:09,560
yet calls you by another name?

171
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,200
I concur.

172
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,280
It is indeed most peculiar.

173
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,800
Where did he acquire these names?

174
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:23,440
They are entirely foreign to my ears.

175
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:26,280
By what name did he address you?

176
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,080
He regarded me

177
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,640
with an unfamiliar eye.

178
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,680
A stark contrast to how he was
when he saw you.

179
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,320
This only serves…

180
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,640
to deepen my suspicions.

181
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,400
I believe he remains clouded
by the spirits.

182
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,320
Cast aside your fears,

183
00:14:56,480 --> 00:14:58,760
lest they erode your reason.

184
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,320
Oh, Master.

185
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,400
Master Klao…

186
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,800
Grant him respite,

187
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,320
and forbid him from
all further indulgence.

188
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,680
In time, he shall return to his true self.

189
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:37,440
Even Thee…

190
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,920
Whatever.

191
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:45,240
I need to find a way back.

192
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:50,320
Students, what are common methods
for main characters

193
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:52,000
to return to the present?

194
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,720
<i>Through a mirror.</i>

195
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:56,680
<i>Drowning and being transported</i>
<i>into a body in a another era.</i>

196
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:59,640
<i>Seeing one's past life</i>
<i>after donning traditional attire.</i>

197
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,000
Drowning.

198
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:05,640
A mirror.

199
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,560
A traditional costume.

200
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:13,680
The master's mind has once again wandered.

201
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:15,800
May a star fall this night.

202
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,160
I shall offer prayers
for his swift restoration.

203
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:22,960
Tonight…

204
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,720
A meteor shower!

205
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,480
I nearly fell, Master!

206
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,400
Yes.

207
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,320
Before I passed out,

208
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:37,080
I saw a shooting star.

209
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,160
Hey, you!

210
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:42,680
This humble servant is named Chuay,
not "You."

211
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:44,480
Whatever.

212
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:49,000
Right now,

213
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:51,960
where's that scary-looking guy?

214
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,520
The…

215
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,800
The deadpan-looking guy.

216
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,560
The Lord…

217
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,800
or whatever he's called.

218
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,160
He has taken his leave

219
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,880
and returned to
High Lord Pichayabhakdi's manor.

220
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:07,720
So…

221
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:10,680
Can you take me back to the woods,

222
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:14,960
to where you found me, Chuay?

223
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,119
Please help me out, Chuay.

224
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,680
That cannot be done, Master.

225
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:22,440
The Lord has commanded me to…

226
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:25,160
prevent any attempt at departure.

227
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,640
Should I disobey,

228
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,600
I would be caned unto my doom.

229
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,400
They cannot be opened.

230
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:57,080
They have been barred from the outside.

231
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,400
We are both confined to these quarters

232
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,280
until the lord returns.

233
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:08,680
This is basically solitary confinement.

234
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:11,040
I'm not shackled by his love!

235
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,040
Get me out of here now!

236
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:15,880
Hey!

237
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,480
They cannot be made to open.

238
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,160
Fine.

239
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,000
You'll see.

240
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,760
I did warn you, Master.

241
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:12,200
The doors cannot be opened.

242
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:14,440
They have been barred from the outside.

243
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:18,840
Fine.

244
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:33,000
Oh, good heavens!

245
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:35,520
A fall from such a height

246
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,880
would certainly shatter
one's bones to dust.

247
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,000
The thought of such an antic

248
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,640
sends a chill through my marrow.

249
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,040
Oh, I'm done.

250
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:13,080
I can't think of anything.

251
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:15,520
My Master,

252
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,720
pray tell me.

253
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,880
Is your condition

254
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:22,040
the result of an indulgence in opium?

255
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,720
If I tell you,

256
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,200
will you take me to the woods?

257
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,320
I cannot, Master.

258
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,400
Master,

259
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:44,720
was your absence
due to an indulgence in opium?

260
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,680
If I tell you,

261
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:57,520
you will take me to the woods, right?

262
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,480
It cannot be done, Master.

263
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,080
I think enough has been said.

264
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,200
My master

265
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:07,880
would not succumb to the allure of opium.

266
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,360
There is a remedy for spirits,

267
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,520
but for the opium

268
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,040
even the Physician has none.

269
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,760
You mean Thee?

270
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,200
I once had back pain.

271
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:25,600
I asked him to buy me some plasters,

272
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:27,720
but he came back with
a bag of plaster mix!

273
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,080
The physician…

274
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:40,240
Master?

275
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,400
What troubles you so?

276
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,320
A stomachache.

277
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,840
Master.

278
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:49,800
It feels like my tummy's gonna explode.

279
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:52,920
A stomachache that
could burst one's belly?

280
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:53,840
Perhaps…

281
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:56,240
Is it abdominal tuberculosis?

282
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:58,240
Yes. Abdominal tuberculosis!

283
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:00,760
Ab-dominoes and everything. Argh!

284
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:01,680
Get the Physician.

285
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,160
Summon the Physician for me.

286
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,280
Yes, Master.

287
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,360
It hurts. I can't.

288
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,600
My stomach's going to burst!

289
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,800
Cuckoo.

290
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:11,320
Cuckoo!

291
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:13,240
Cuckoo.

292
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,720
Cuckoo!

293
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,080
Cuckoo.

294
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,040
Cuckoo!

295
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,440
Cuckoo!

296
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Quite a rascal.

297
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:11,000
But I'm worse.

298
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:29,800
Ow!

299
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:43,920
This way.

300
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,080
Make haste, I beg you.

301
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,360
What is it, Chuay?

302
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,320
He just arrived,

303
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,640
yet you seek the physician
only after nightfall?

304
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,040
<i>You again.</i>

305
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:54,760
<i>Do people in the old days</i>
<i>have nothing better to do?</i>

306
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,160
It is Master Klao, my Lord.

307
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:58,280
Such is his distress that he recoils.

308
00:23:58,360 --> 00:24:00,400
I think it's abdominal tuberculosis.

309
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,840
Could such a disease be possible?

310
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:05,120
His restless spirit
showed no sign of waning.

311
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,040
Who is watching over him?

312
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:15,200
Chuay, you have been deceived by him.

313
00:24:28,360 --> 00:24:29,360
Klao.

314
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:33,200
What brings you to these shadows?

315
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:44,480
Pun!

316
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:45,720
Yes. I'm safe now.

317
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:50,640
Pun.

318
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:52,600
What are you doing here?

319
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:53,560
Gosh…

320
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:56,240
You know what's happening, don't you?

321
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,480
Klao…

322
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:03,160
Jom's words were true.
You have lost your wits.

323
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:06,480
Hey, Pun.

324
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:08,240
No, don't do me like this.

325
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,360
Klao, it pains me.

326
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,480
Jom!

327
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:14,200
Where are you?

328
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:15,360
Jom!

329
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:26,080
Oh, Nakun?

330
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,160
Have you eaten yet?

331
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,600
I'm starving.

332
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:30,600
Nakun, try this.

333
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:32,160
It's the new mint flavor.

334
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:33,560
If you don't mind…

335
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,680
-How is it?
-Gosh…

336
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,280
Refreshing breath,

337
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:42,000
nice and clean.

338
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,520
What kind of prank is this?

339
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:49,080
Thee.

340
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:51,200
Stop pulling pranks on Nakun.

341
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,480
This isn't funny at all.

342
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Eat it yourself.

343
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:59,200
He mocks me for liking mint chocolate.

344
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,280
It's fine, Pun.

345
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:07,040
This is nothing.

346
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:09,480
He always does stuff like this.

347
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,360
Come on, Pun.

348
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,960
You're mad like I pranked you.

349
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,440
I'll eat it. Here.

350
00:26:15,520 --> 00:26:16,760
Hey, don't.

351
00:26:16,840 --> 00:26:17,680
It's fine.

352
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:19,160
It's nothing.

353
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:20,800
Well, enjoy.

354
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:21,880
I just ate some.

355
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:25,960
Yeah, eat up!

356
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:27,800
-Look at him.
-You--

357
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,000
You're still mad at me?

358
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:31,640
<i>Pun doesn't pull pranks on others.</i>

359
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:37,760
<i>If this is really him,</i>
<i>he wouldn't be deceiving me.</i>

360
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:40,360
<i>Why?</i>

361
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:43,000
<i>Traveling through time isn't enough?</i>

362
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:46,200
<i>Why is it someone who looks like</i>
<i>my friend and fraternity brother?</i>

363
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:56,000
Klao. Return to the manor at once.

364
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:57,640
Let go!

365
00:26:58,760 --> 00:27:00,280
I told you I'm not Klao!

366
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:03,280
Stop calling me by that name!

367
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:05,920
Master Klao!

368
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Master.

369
00:27:07,080 --> 00:27:08,200
Trouble him no further.

370
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:10,160
Allow him his solitude.

371
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:13,640
Leave him to the quiet counsel
of his own thoughts.

372
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,000
I shall attend to him shortly.

373
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,080
<i>Of course.</i>

374
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:33,280
<i>Why would there be a meteor shower?</i>

375
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,640
<i>It doesn't happen</i>
<i>every night, does it?</i>

376
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:38,480
<i>I won't get to return home, will I?</i>

377
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:41,040
<i>Will my mom be surprised?</i>

378
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:44,000
<i>What about the real Thee and Pun?</i>
<i>How will they be?</i>

379
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:55,560
You're here to drag me back?

380
00:27:57,840 --> 00:27:59,800
I am here for the sake of companionship.

381
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,560
Draw your breath slowly,

382
00:28:35,040 --> 00:28:36,360
or you will faint.

383
00:29:20,320 --> 00:29:21,160
Hey.

384
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:23,600
Who were those two?

385
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:26,280
Jom and Kaew,

386
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:29,560
companions since our youth.

387
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:36,560
You…

388
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:38,200
You're not lying, are you?

389
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:49,800
I harbor no deceit when I speak to you.

390
00:29:57,520 --> 00:29:58,400
Thank you.

391
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:01,480
Thanks.

392
00:30:29,760 --> 00:30:30,880
Rest now.

393
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:34,720
Long and undisturbed repose
is what is required.

394
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:35,920
Fret not,

395
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:39,000
for you shall return to
your senses in no time.

396
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:46,320
Can I ask you something?

397
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,240
Where are we?

398
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:06,800
This is the small manor,

399
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:10,760
situated on
the estate of High Lord Pichayabhakdi,

400
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,640
my father.

401
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:17,120
Why can't you remember this?

402
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:19,480
And…

403
00:31:20,240 --> 00:31:21,440
what province?

404
00:31:26,240 --> 00:31:27,080
Province?

405
00:31:30,360 --> 00:31:31,440
What city?

406
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:34,840
Is it in Bangkok or what?

407
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:41,880
Do you speak of…

408
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,000
Phra Nakhon?

409
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:48,080
Phra Nakhon…

410
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,920
Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya?

411
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:54,520
No.

412
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:58,760
Ayothaya Si Ram Thep Nakhon.

413
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:00,440
And…

414
00:32:01,560 --> 00:32:02,480
Day?

415
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:05,040
What day is it?

416
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:06,920
Sunday.

417
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:08,440
What month…

418
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,800
and year?

419
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:13,600
Year Six of the Decennial Cycle.

420
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:17,120
or 986 of the Lesser Era.

421
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,160
The Year of the Rat.

422
00:32:19,600 --> 00:32:20,960
The Second Lunar Month.

423
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:23,360
The First Waxing Moon.

424
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:25,560
Sunday.

425
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,640
The reign of King Songtham.

426
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:39,400
KING SONGTHAM

427
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:42,200
<i>Who is King Songtham?</i>

428
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:44,200
<i>I just know King Naresuan, King Narai.</i>

429
00:32:44,280 --> 00:32:46,120
ROYAL CHRONICLES OF AYUTTHAYA KINGDOM

430
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:47,080
<i>Lesser Era?</i>

431
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,520
13 KINGS
SUPHANNAPHUM DYNASTY

432
00:32:48,600 --> 00:32:51,680
<i>What year in modern calendar</i>
<i>is this Lesser Era?</i>

433
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:54,320
<i>See, Nakun?</i>
<i>This is why you failed the exam!</i>

434
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:56,440
<i>Why didn't you study harder?</i>

435
00:32:57,720 --> 00:33:01,640
<i>I've really traveled back</i>
<i>to the Ayutthaya period, haven't I?</i>

436
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:03,800
<i>Around 300-400 years ago.</i>

437
00:33:08,040 --> 00:33:10,160
Have you sustained any injuries?

438
00:33:24,320 --> 00:33:25,920
Hey, what are you doing?

439
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:53,120
Remain still for a moment.

440
00:34:16,719 --> 00:34:17,800
<i>Do men of this age</i>

441
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:20,840
<i>actually look this handsome?</i>

442
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:24,560
<i>Hey!</i>

443
00:34:24,639 --> 00:34:26,040
<i>No, no, no, no.</i>

444
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:28,080
<i>He's 400 years older than me.</i>

445
00:34:28,159 --> 00:34:29,280
<i>He may be good-looking,</i>

446
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:31,760
<i>but he's like</i>
<i>my great-great-great ancestor!</i>

447
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:38,760
Klao?

448
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:43,679
Is it that your memory of me has faded,

449
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:47,480
or do you harbor grievances against me?

450
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:58,640
No matter.

451
00:35:01,760 --> 00:35:03,320
It matters not, now.

452
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:06,160
Rest,

453
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:10,320
and adhere to
the physician's medicinal instructions,

454
00:35:11,520 --> 00:35:13,120
and you shall recover.

455
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:12,600
<i>Let's say.</i>

456
00:36:12,680 --> 00:36:13,800
<i>Let's just say…</i>

457
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:16,720
<i>I've really traveled back</i>
<i>to the Ayutthaya period.</i>

458
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:17,960
<i>The question is…</i>

459
00:36:18,040 --> 00:36:19,240
<i>Why me?</i>

460
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,240
<i>Why here?</i>

461
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:25,720
What promise did you make, and to whom?

462
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,920
Someone from the past
awaits its fulfillment.

463
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:30,400
Why did I have to get into this faculty?

464
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:32,800
Can we go back in time and change this?

465
00:36:32,880 --> 00:36:34,920
What if time, as we know it,

466
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,840
doesn't move linearly?

467
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:39,600
It loops back,

468
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:40,600
becoming a cycle.

469
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:42,160
This suggests that

470
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:45,360
the concepts of past
and future lives might actually exist.

471
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:47,360
<i>Traveling back in time</i>

472
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:49,640
<i>and becoming myself in my past life?</i>

473
00:36:50,120 --> 00:36:50,960
<i>No way.</i>

474
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:52,960
<i>That's insane.</i>

475
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:55,440
<i>It's impossible, right?</i>

476
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:57,480
<i>That's way too much like fiction.</i>

477
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:07,800
<i>All right. If I can't go back right now,</i>

478
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:09,760
<i>I guess I have to become Klao.</i>

479
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,880
<i>I guess you're Klao now, Nakun!</i>

480
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:36,200
Are you awake from your slumber?

481
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:50,920
Would you refresh yourself, Master?

482
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:53,600
Sure.

483
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:56,720
Does the bathroom have a shower

484
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:58,720
or a bathtub?

485
00:38:10,680 --> 00:38:14,480
<i>There are no bathrooms</i>
<i>in the Ayutthaya period?</i>

486
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,680
<i>So cold! I refuse.</i>

487
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:29,240
<i>I won't shower no matter what.</i>

488
00:38:34,040 --> 00:38:34,880
Chuay.

489
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:39,200
Can you heat up the water for me?

490
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:44,320
Please?

491
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:47,000
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover…

492
00:38:47,080 --> 00:38:49,160
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover.

493
00:38:49,240 --> 00:38:51,680
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover…

494
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:53,760
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover.

495
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:55,280
Master has gone mad,

496
00:38:55,360 --> 00:38:56,880
yet he shall recover.

497
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:57,920
Chuay.

498
00:38:58,760 --> 00:38:59,600
Yes, Master?

499
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:00,640
What is this?

500
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:01,720
Is it a makeup brush?

501
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:20,640
Master.

502
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:24,640
The trousers you wear,
are they from the Farangi?

503
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:27,600
You mean my boxers?

504
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,600
Yes, they're from Farangi.

505
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,800
Oh, but…

506
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:36,040
Don't let anyone touch them.

507
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:37,880
Don't let anyone wash them either.

508
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:39,680
They're extremely important.

509
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:40,880
My personal belongings,

510
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:42,840
and they were expensive.

511
00:39:42,920 --> 00:39:44,320
It's also a one-off.

512
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:45,400
Yes, Master.

513
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:49,560
I shall not lay my hands on your "boxers."

514
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:54,960
Gosh…

515
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:57,240
All right.

516
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:02,760
Hair curls.

517
00:40:03,480 --> 00:40:05,120
Check out those commas.

518
00:40:05,200 --> 00:40:06,920
It's the Korean style,

519
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:10,800
Come on.

520
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:13,200
I'm craving breakfast.

521
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:21,560
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover.

522
00:40:21,640 --> 00:40:24,120
Master has gone mad,
yet he shall recover…

523
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:27,800
Await me, Master.

524
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:30,840
Your rice, Master.

525
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:32,560
Thank you.

526
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,000
Feast, Master.

527
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:47,080
Where are my spoon and fork?

528
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:49,120
You want me to eat with my hands?

529
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,640
Here, Master.

530
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:01,320
Yes, Master…

531
00:41:02,320 --> 00:41:03,160
Yes, Master.

532
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:32,640
Sai poured her whole heart into this meal.

533
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:34,120
Indeed, Master.

534
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:36,840
Your name is Sai?

535
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:38,520
Yes, Master.

536
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:40,520
She is my beloved.

537
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:43,440
Your beloved?

538
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:49,040
Chuay, how old are you?

539
00:41:49,120 --> 00:41:50,760
Why did you get a wife so quickly?

540
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,560
This is nothing strange.

541
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:55,480
My peers have already founded
their own lineages.

542
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:57,400
And…

543
00:41:57,480 --> 00:41:58,760
Klao…

544
00:41:58,840 --> 00:41:59,680
Sorry.

545
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:02,280
What about me?

546
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:04,040
Master Klao…

547
00:42:05,280 --> 00:42:06,720
You have even forgotten about…

548
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:09,000
I have one?

549
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:10,480
No, Master.

550
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:12,800
What a relief.

551
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:19,000
Does no trace of it remain?

552
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:20,440
Well…

553
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,840
I'm starting to recall some of it now.

554
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:25,960
Grant us your questions,

555
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:28,080
for we are both ready to answer.

556
00:42:28,160 --> 00:42:29,520
Sai and I

557
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:31,680
shall aid you
in regaining memories, Master.

558
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:35,640
Well…

559
00:42:38,520 --> 00:42:39,960
That deadpan Lord…

560
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:42,160
is he taken?

561
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:50,160
<i>Our Lord is a gracious</i>

562
00:42:50,240 --> 00:42:51,480
<i>and generous soul,</i>

563
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:53,760
<i>much like High Lord Pichayabhakdi,</i>

564
00:42:53,840 --> 00:42:54,880
<i>his father.</i>

565
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:56,840
He is devoid of arrogance,

566
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:59,440
treating even the lowliest
with unwavering respect.

567
00:42:59,520 --> 00:43:01,960
<i>He bears a most refined composure,</i>

568
00:43:02,680 --> 00:43:04,480
<i>befitting his striking visage.</i>

569
00:43:26,040 --> 00:43:27,320
By the way…

570
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:28,920
This Lord…

571
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:30,240
How old is he?

572
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:32,480
He is your elder by a year.

573
00:43:33,160 --> 00:43:35,960
He will reach his 21st year
in the course of this cycle.

574
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:37,320
Twenty-one…

575
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:41,080
Handsome, with a wealthy father…

576
00:43:41,840 --> 00:43:45,000
He's not old by the standards of this era.

577
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:48,000
I guess he's married, right?

578
00:43:48,080 --> 00:43:51,080
He has yet to establish
a household of his own.

579
00:43:51,160 --> 00:43:52,480
Really?

580
00:43:52,560 --> 00:43:53,920
Despite his good looks,

581
00:43:54,720 --> 00:43:56,080
he's still not married?

582
00:43:57,440 --> 00:43:59,560
Such is not the case, Master.

583
00:43:59,640 --> 00:44:02,080
<i>A lord of such striking beauty</i>

584
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:05,840
<i>holds half the maidens of the capital</i>
<i>in longing for his hand.</i>

585
00:44:19,080 --> 00:44:19,920
<i>Desired by many,</i>

586
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:22,160
<i>he is yet moved by none.</i>

587
00:44:26,320 --> 00:44:28,240
He's not keen on commitment, is he?

588
00:44:28,320 --> 00:44:29,920
He is not, Master.

589
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:32,000
He takes no liking to any maiden,

590
00:44:32,560 --> 00:44:34,480
nor does he seek

591
00:44:34,560 --> 00:44:36,280
the company of women of the night.

592
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:41,640
Is he gay?

593
00:44:43,720 --> 00:44:44,680
No, Master.

594
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:46,400
He is not gray.

595
00:44:47,040 --> 00:44:48,120
He is sharp, not dull.

596
00:44:50,320 --> 00:44:52,520
He harms no soul,

597
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:54,880
nor acts in a shady manner.

598
00:44:58,080 --> 00:44:59,480
I get it now. Continue.

599
00:45:00,960 --> 00:45:04,360
He seeks to devote every effort
toward the betterment of the land.

600
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,440
Like doing work?

601
00:45:06,520 --> 00:45:07,800
What work?

602
00:45:07,880 --> 00:45:10,560
<i>He serves in the ranks of</i>
<i>the Royal Patrol Division</i>

603
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,800
<i>of the Ministry of the Capital.</i>

604
00:45:13,920 --> 00:45:16,560
Cease this.
What manner of quarrel is this?

605
00:45:16,640 --> 00:45:19,240
Oh, so he's kinda like security?

606
00:45:20,480 --> 00:45:23,480
He safeguards the populace

607
00:45:24,360 --> 00:45:27,600
and suppresses
all manner of banditry and vice.

608
00:45:28,320 --> 00:45:29,920
He is indebted to us…

609
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:31,320
a gambling debt, my Lord.

610
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:35,160
Yet, your grievances
do not excuse this brawling.

611
00:45:35,240 --> 00:45:36,080
Leave.

612
00:45:36,680 --> 00:45:38,400
Claim your recompense on the morrow.

613
00:45:42,920 --> 00:45:44,240
Forsake the wager,

614
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:47,440
and dedicate yourself to honest trade.

615
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:50,280
Deliver unto them
the payment on the morrow.

616
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:54,080
Oh, he's been working so hard

617
00:45:54,160 --> 00:45:56,360
that he doesn't have time for dating.

618
00:45:57,200 --> 00:45:58,200
I mean…

619
00:45:58,280 --> 00:45:59,520
Seeking a partner.

620
00:46:01,240 --> 00:46:03,560
You might well put it that way, indeed.

621
00:46:03,640 --> 00:46:04,960
The lord usually

622
00:46:05,640 --> 00:46:06,680
takes no heed

623
00:46:07,480 --> 00:46:09,280
of the welfare of others.

624
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:14,040
His concern is reserved solely for…

625
00:46:14,120 --> 00:46:15,640
you, Master Klao.

626
00:46:18,520 --> 00:46:19,680
Indeed, Master.

627
00:46:20,480 --> 00:46:22,240
In your absence,

628
00:46:22,320 --> 00:46:25,240
the lord summoned us all
for a stern interrogation.

629
00:46:25,880 --> 00:46:28,560
His voice resounded across the estate.

630
00:46:30,080 --> 00:46:30,920
I saw that.

631
00:46:31,920 --> 00:46:34,160
If that is the case, Master,

632
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:36,120
do not depart from us again,

633
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:39,400
for I fear the lord
may fall into worry once more.

634
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:53,120
To regain one's memory

635
00:46:53,720 --> 00:46:56,240
requires a long period of restoration.

636
00:46:56,320 --> 00:46:58,560
I cannot say with certainty how long.

637
00:47:01,640 --> 00:47:04,920
Yet you are the finest physician
the capital has ever known.

638
00:47:05,800 --> 00:47:08,640
Surely some remedy exists
to aid his recovery.

639
00:47:08,720 --> 00:47:11,200
I accept your praise with gratitude.

640
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:13,720
Yet whichever physician you consult,

641
00:47:14,480 --> 00:47:16,080
the conclusion remains immutable.

642
00:47:19,160 --> 00:47:22,280
I shall provide
a remedy to strengthen the mind then.

643
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:26,480
Shall we see to him at the manor?

644
00:47:26,560 --> 00:47:27,680
I concur,

645
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:30,040
though only on the morrow.

646
00:47:30,840 --> 00:47:32,720
The capital calls this day.

647
00:47:32,800 --> 00:47:34,000
The capital?

648
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:35,920
Who requires your summons?

649
00:47:41,840 --> 00:47:44,040
I need to procure medicines
from the Farangi.

650
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:46,320
No one summons me.

651
00:47:48,720 --> 00:47:50,280
Is another day agreeable to you?

652
00:47:51,680 --> 00:47:53,800
Klao's condition remains precarious.

653
00:47:54,640 --> 00:47:56,120
You…

654
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:57,440
Regarding Klao's affairs,

655
00:47:57,520 --> 00:47:59,640
your heart is more troubled
than your own.

656
00:48:04,600 --> 00:48:06,440
Phop, the hour of joy calls!

657
00:48:08,240 --> 00:48:10,040
-Klao, stay!
-Klao, mind your footing!

658
00:48:13,080 --> 00:48:14,280
Masters.

659
00:48:14,360 --> 00:48:16,040
Be wary, Masters.

660
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:18,080
Masters.

661
00:48:21,880 --> 00:48:23,880
Pursue me, if your legs are stout.

662
00:48:26,720 --> 00:48:27,560
Crash!

663
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:30,760
Jom, this is for you.

664
00:48:30,840 --> 00:48:32,040
Away with it.

665
00:48:32,920 --> 00:48:33,800
I am no lady.

666
00:48:37,680 --> 00:48:38,520
-Master!
-Master!

667
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:40,720
-Klao!
-Master!

668
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:42,200
Master…

669
00:48:45,120 --> 00:48:46,640
Klao, you are but a whimper.

670
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:49,040
Seek solace in your lady mother's skirts.

671
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:56,800
Jom, cease this mockery.

672
00:48:56,880 --> 00:48:58,600
Heed your manners.

673
00:48:59,280 --> 00:49:01,880
You know full well
he is bereft of a mother's care.

674
00:49:07,680 --> 00:49:09,280
We shall escort you to the manor.

675
00:49:09,360 --> 00:49:10,200
No need.

676
00:49:10,760 --> 00:49:12,000
I will attend to him.

677
00:49:32,400 --> 00:49:33,960
It is truly a grievous thing,

678
00:49:34,040 --> 00:49:36,640
to have been orphaned of a mother's love.

679
00:49:41,960 --> 00:49:43,160
Jom.

680
00:49:43,760 --> 00:49:45,080
I propose that

681
00:49:45,160 --> 00:49:46,760
we attend to him together.

682
00:49:47,400 --> 00:49:50,320
I have prepared
his beloved dessert, <i>khanom tom.</i>

683
00:49:50,400 --> 00:49:52,600
See to him quickly,
before the freshness fades.

684
00:49:55,720 --> 00:49:56,800
On the morrow.

685
00:49:57,800 --> 00:50:00,960
Your affections
have been so lavish that Klao is spoiled.

686
00:50:01,040 --> 00:50:03,040
Observe the fruits
of lavish indulgence.

687
00:50:03,120 --> 00:50:06,440
To find his company, seek breweries
and the ladies of the night.

688
00:50:06,520 --> 00:50:09,280
He is favored by fortune
to have found his way back.

689
00:50:10,160 --> 00:50:13,240
I have long felt the urge to caution him,

690
00:50:13,320 --> 00:50:15,560
but solely out of deference
to your feelings,

691
00:50:16,400 --> 00:50:18,440
I refrained from speaking.

692
00:50:33,040 --> 00:50:34,240
I am utterly confounded.

693
00:50:34,320 --> 00:50:36,800
You've forgotten how to dress yourself
and even eat.

694
00:50:36,880 --> 00:50:39,320
At least you still retain
the ability to dine.

695
00:50:39,400 --> 00:50:41,200
Else I would fear for your very life.

696
00:50:45,960 --> 00:50:47,600
Master! Master!

697
00:50:48,520 --> 00:50:50,480
Your attire is disheveled.

698
00:50:50,560 --> 00:50:52,320
Allow me to assist you, Master.

699
00:50:52,400 --> 00:50:53,440
Come on.

700
00:50:54,080 --> 00:50:56,280
If you're not gonna let me
wear my trousers,

701
00:50:56,360 --> 00:50:59,320
then let me wear them like this.
They're too tight.

702
00:50:59,400 --> 00:51:00,360
It cannot be done.

703
00:51:00,440 --> 00:51:02,080
Grant me this one request, Master.

704
00:51:03,480 --> 00:51:05,480
-Allow me to assist you.
-Gosh.

705
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:06,680
Master Klao.

706
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:16,360
What stays your hand, Chuay?

707
00:51:16,440 --> 00:51:17,680
The Lord has summoned you.

708
00:51:17,760 --> 00:51:19,840
Oh, dear, he is summoning us.

709
00:51:21,640 --> 00:51:23,960
Make haste, for His Excellency awaits.

710
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:25,240
As predicted.

711
00:51:25,320 --> 00:51:26,560
His Excellency awaits.

712
00:51:26,640 --> 00:51:29,280
Gosh, why did you have to
repeat his words?

713
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:30,920
Master.

714
00:51:31,440 --> 00:51:33,000
If you find the lord stern,

715
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:35,600
you shall find his father, His Excellency,

716
00:51:35,680 --> 00:51:36,880
even more formidable.

717
00:51:36,960 --> 00:51:38,360
I beg of you, Master.

718
00:51:38,440 --> 00:51:41,920
-Attend to your attire, Master.
-Come on, get up.

719
00:51:44,600 --> 00:51:45,440
Fine!

720
00:51:56,240 --> 00:51:57,520
Troubled throat?

721
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:23,840
That is Kong,

722
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:25,920
the lord's servant.

723
00:52:39,400 --> 00:52:40,280
Hello.

724
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:45,880
Hello?

725
00:52:47,360 --> 00:52:49,080
Do you speak a foreign tongue, Klao?

726
00:52:49,160 --> 00:52:51,560
Or is that
the customary greeting of Phichit?

727
00:52:52,640 --> 00:52:53,480
<i>Phichit…</i>

728
00:52:54,160 --> 00:52:55,480
<i>Klao's from Phichit?</i>

729
00:52:56,440 --> 00:52:57,320
Be seated.

730
00:52:58,320 --> 00:52:59,720
Take your place beside Phop.

731
00:52:59,800 --> 00:53:01,040
Understood.

732
00:53:10,880 --> 00:53:13,120
Phop has mentioned your affliction.

733
00:53:13,200 --> 00:53:14,960
How fares your recovery?

734
00:53:15,760 --> 00:53:16,880
Has it taken its leave?

735
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:21,880
The servants claim that

736
00:53:21,960 --> 00:53:23,200
you have gone mad.

737
00:53:23,760 --> 00:53:24,600
Is it so?

738
00:53:26,600 --> 00:53:28,520
Have you lost all your memories?

739
00:53:28,600 --> 00:53:29,520
Good heavens.

740
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:32,040
Who…

741
00:53:32,120 --> 00:53:33,000
Who am I?

742
00:53:34,360 --> 00:53:35,560
By what name am I known?

743
00:53:43,360 --> 00:53:44,800
Is your mind a complete void?

744
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:52,960
It appears
he has not only lost his memories,

745
00:53:53,040 --> 00:53:55,680
but he has also
lost his command of language.

746
00:53:56,600 --> 00:53:58,800
Could this man
truly not be Dear Klao?

747
00:54:00,560 --> 00:54:02,440
Is this an apparition in his likeness?

748
00:54:03,920 --> 00:54:05,600
-Oh, dear.
-Go not near him.

749
00:54:07,920 --> 00:54:08,760
Bud.

750
00:54:09,160 --> 00:54:10,000
Euang.

751
00:54:12,120 --> 00:54:14,560
Cease your jesting for now.

752
00:54:16,680 --> 00:54:17,840
Dearest Klao,

753
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:20,480
my name is Lady Prayong,

754
00:54:21,240 --> 00:54:22,920
Lord Phop's mother

755
00:54:23,880 --> 00:54:26,560
and the primary consort of
High Lord Pichayabhakdi.

756
00:54:29,720 --> 00:54:31,880
On the morrow, we shall visit the temple.

757
00:54:31,960 --> 00:54:33,600
Kindly join me on this journey

758
00:54:34,280 --> 00:54:37,280
so that misfortunes may be dispelled.

759
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:43,800
The current moment is ill-suited,

760
00:54:45,120 --> 00:54:46,320
for he is still feeble.

761
00:54:47,080 --> 00:54:49,440
The physician forbids him
from leaving the estate.

762
00:54:49,520 --> 00:54:51,000
It is a journey to the temple.

763
00:54:51,080 --> 00:54:53,000
What harm could possibly befall him?

764
00:54:54,720 --> 00:54:55,920
Dearest Klao.

765
00:54:56,000 --> 00:54:57,480
Will you join us to the temple?

766
00:54:58,640 --> 00:54:59,560
With pleasure.

767
00:55:02,400 --> 00:55:03,840
Behold.

768
00:55:04,560 --> 00:55:06,160
This brings him immense joy.

769
00:55:06,800 --> 00:55:08,560
Abide by your mother's words.

770
00:55:09,240 --> 00:55:10,520
You, too, are to join us

771
00:55:11,520 --> 00:55:12,760
and accompany him.

772
00:55:13,600 --> 00:55:14,680
Understood, Father.

773
00:55:16,640 --> 00:55:19,320
It is my decree that
he vacate the small manor

774
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:21,520
and take up residence here.

775
00:55:23,120 --> 00:55:24,440
It's okay.

776
00:55:27,880 --> 00:55:30,400
I'd rather stay at the small manor.

777
00:55:31,800 --> 00:55:34,160
I also don't want to trouble you.

778
00:55:35,200 --> 00:55:36,800
You shall seek shelter here,

779
00:55:36,880 --> 00:55:39,120
where your well-being
can be properly overseen.

780
00:55:39,760 --> 00:55:40,880
Prior to his passing,

781
00:55:41,760 --> 00:55:43,360
Lord Preechapiban,

782
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:44,760
your father,

783
00:55:45,720 --> 00:55:47,200
left you in my keeping.

784
00:55:47,840 --> 00:55:49,240
Should you vanish once more,

785
00:55:50,200 --> 00:55:51,840
your father's spirit

786
00:55:51,920 --> 00:55:53,520
shall find no rest.

787
00:55:57,400 --> 00:55:58,240
Chuay.

788
00:55:58,320 --> 00:56:00,960
Retrieve your master's essential
belongings

789
00:56:01,480 --> 00:56:03,320
and convey them here before nightfall.

790
00:56:04,200 --> 00:56:05,040
Yes, my Lord.

791
00:56:07,480 --> 00:56:08,960
<i>Klao's father has already died.</i>

792
00:56:09,920 --> 00:56:11,840
<i>What was the cause of his death?</i>

793
00:56:11,920 --> 00:56:14,560
<i>Why did he leave Klao with His Excellency?</i>

794
00:56:22,440 --> 00:56:24,040
<i>Everyone's staring at me harshly.</i>

795
00:56:24,120 --> 00:56:24,960
<i>Why?</i>

796
00:56:25,680 --> 00:56:26,520
<i>Gosh.</i>

797
00:56:26,600 --> 00:56:28,760
<i>How am I supposed to pretend to be him?</i>

798
00:56:28,840 --> 00:56:30,120
<i>I know nothing about Klao.</i>

799
00:56:40,160 --> 00:56:42,000
Our current proximity is indeed ideal,

800
00:56:44,400 --> 00:56:46,680
for it allows me
to keep a close eye on you.

801
00:56:47,600 --> 00:56:49,200
<i>Isn't this a bit weird?</i>

802
00:56:49,280 --> 00:56:51,760
<i>Are you sure</i>
<i>we're just friends from childhood?</i>

803
00:56:52,640 --> 00:56:54,440
<i>This freaking Lord…</i>

804
00:56:54,520 --> 00:56:56,160
<i>What is he to Klao?</i>

805
00:57:10,600 --> 00:57:11,600
Do eat.

806
00:57:12,200 --> 00:57:14,160
You have withered in our absence.

807
00:57:22,800 --> 00:57:23,840
<i>Don't tell me…</i>

808
00:57:24,840 --> 00:57:26,280
<i>Don't tell me that…</i>

809
00:57:52,600 --> 00:57:53,480
Father!

810
00:57:53,560 --> 00:57:55,280
<i>Klao's father is dead.</i>

811
00:57:55,360 --> 00:57:57,080
<i>Whose voice roars so loudly yonder?</i>

812
00:57:58,200 --> 00:57:59,280
<i>Fortune teller!</i>

813
00:57:59,360 --> 00:58:00,200
Klao!

814
00:58:00,280 --> 00:58:03,960
You ought not to run about on your own.
Someone might do you harm.

815
00:58:04,040 --> 00:58:06,640
You are the one
who harms me.

816
00:58:07,160 --> 00:58:09,720
<i>Suffers from amnesia</i>
<i>and remembers nothing of himself…</i>

817
00:58:09,800 --> 00:58:12,920
Should I ever forget you,
what will you do?

818
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:14,600
Nothing.

819
00:58:14,680 --> 00:58:16,120
Even if you forget me,

820
00:58:16,200 --> 00:58:17,680
I shall care for you still.

821
00:58:18,360 --> 00:58:20,200
I told you not to come in yet, Chuay.

822
00:58:22,920 --> 00:58:24,360
<i>Forgive me for this morning.</i>

823
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:27,680
<i>Do not hold it against me.</i>
